note as N1
  Contract
  - apply() is only ever called when the project is in the exact state the command was created against
    (History guarantees this by strict LIFO order), so apply()/revert() never need to validate or fail.
  - apply() followed by revert() restores the project bit-for-bit (except Frame.revision, which only increases).
  - Commands own all data they need (they never keep references into the project). Frames are addressed by FrameId,
    layers by LayerId (both stable), never by index; the indices stored in commands are only insert / remove positions.
  - Commands never touch Selection, Viewport, ToolOptions, the brush library or the file on disk.
    The few operations that must also move the selection (Move cells, Paste, Import) hand a SelectionChange to the History,
    which stores it NEXT TO the command and returns it from undo() / redo() (see the rules below).
end note

note as N2
  Rules
  - execute(cmd): cmd.apply(project); then record_applied(cmd).   execute_with_selection(cmd, project, sel): the same, then record_applied_with_selection.
  - record_applied(cmd): used when the change is already in the project (strokes, fills, moves).
      1. redo_stack.clear()  - if clean_marker is Some(m) with m > undo_stack.len(), set clean_marker = None.
      2. undo_stack.push(HistoryEntry{ cmd, selection: None })   (record_applied_with_selection stores Some(sel))
      3. if undo_stack.len() > limit: undo_stack.remove(0); clean_marker = clean_marker.and_then(|m| m.checked_sub(1))
         (a marker that falls off the bottom becomes None = "always dirty").
  - undo(): pop undo_stack, entry.cmd.revert(project), push onto redo_stack, return UndoStep{ label, selection: entry.selection.before }.
    None if empty.   redo(): pop redo_stack, entry.cmd.apply(project), push onto undo_stack, return UndoStep{ label, selection: entry.selection.after }.
  - The caller (EditorSession) applies UndoStep.selection with Selection::restore() when it is Some. Entries without a SelectionChange leave the selection alone.
  - mark_clean(): clean_marker = Some(undo_stack.len())   (called right after a successful save of the .aspr).
  - is_dirty(): clean_marker != Some(undo_stack.len())    (a brand-new project starts with clean_marker = Some(0)).
  - EditorSession::undo()/redo() always dispatches ToolEvent::Cancel to the active tool FIRST, so a running stroke is committed
    and a running Move drag is rolled back (a drag / polygon preview discarded) before the history is touched.
end note

note as N3
  apply : fidx = timeline.index_of(frame_id).unwrap(); lidx = frame.index_of_layer(layer_id).unwrap();
          for ch in ink_changes (in order)  frame.set_ink(layer_id, ch.coord, ch.after);
          for ch in fill_changes (in order) frame.set_fill(layer_id, ch.coord, ch.after);
          then timeline.select(fidx); frame.select_layer(lidx) so the user always SEES what was changed.
  revert: same loops in REVERSE order writing ch.before; then timeline.select(fidx); frame.select_layer(lidx).
  Used by: Paint cells, Erase cells, Fill cells, Move cells, Cut, "Clear selection".
end note

note as N4
  new(): returns None when the frame does not exist or its background already equals `after` (nothing to record).
  apply : frame.set_background(after)    revert: frame.set_background(before)
  "Apply to all frames" in the colour dialog = CompositeCommand("Set background (all frames)") containing one
  SetFrameBackgroundCommand per frame whose colour differs, so one Ctrl+Z restores every frame.
end note

note as N5
  blank_after(project, i): frame = Frame::blank(project.alloc_frame_id(), canvas, background of frame i) = ONE blank layer "Layer 1"; index = i + 1.
  duplicate(project, i) : frame = frame[i].duplicate_as(project.alloc_frame_id()) = copy of ALL layers and the background; index = i + 1.
  selected_before = timeline.selected_index() at creation time.
  apply : timeline.insert(index, frame.clone()); timeline.select(index)
  revert: timeline.remove(index); timeline.select(min(selected_before, len - 1))
end note

note as N6
  new() fails with CannotRemoveLastFrame when timeline.len() == 1 (the Delete button is also disabled then).
  apply : timeline.remove(index); timeline.select(min(index, len - 1))
  revert: timeline.insert(index, frame.clone()); timeline.select(selected_before)
  The command keeps the whole frame (every layer) so undo restores it completely.
end note

note as N7
  Created by drag-and-drop in the frame list (from = dragged index, to = index after removal, see Timeline::move_frame).
  Not created when from == to.
  apply : timeline.move_frame(from, to); timeline.select(to)
  revert: timeline.move_frame(to, from); timeline.select(selected_before)
end note

note as N8
  Created when the FPS field or the Loop checkbox changes (one command per committed edit: Enter / focus loss / drag release
  for FPS, one click for Loop - not one per keystroke). Not created when nothing differs.
  apply : timeline.fps = after_fps; timeline.looping = after_looping
  revert: timeline.fps = before_fps; timeline.looping = before_looping
end note

note as N9
  Layer list commands (all address the frame by FrameId and select that frame so the change is visible)
  AddLayerCommand
    blank_above(project, frame_id): layer = Layer::blank(frame.alloc_layer_id(), "Layer <id>", canvas); index = active + 1.
    duplicate(project, frame_id, i): copy of layers[i] with a fresh LayerId, name "<name> copy"; index = i + 1.
    with_layer(project, frame_id, layer): a ready-made layer (paste, import); index = active + 1; the caller allocated layer.id.
    All three fail with TooManyLayers when the frame already holds 64 layers.   active_before = frame.active_index().
    apply : frame.insert_layer(index, layer.clone()); frame.select_layer(index)
    revert: frame.remove_layer(index); frame.select_layer(min(active_before, len - 1))
  DeleteLayerCommand  (new() fails with CannotRemoveLastLayer when the frame has one layer; the Delete button is disabled then)
    apply : frame.remove_layer(index); frame.select_layer(min(index, len - 1))
    revert: frame.insert_layer(index, layer.clone()); frame.select_layer(active_before)
  MoveLayerCommand (drag and drop in the Layers panel; from / to are layer indices, bottom = 0, `to` = index after removal)
    apply : frame.move_layer(from, to); frame.select_layer(to)      revert: frame.move_layer(to, from); frame.select_layer(active_before)
end note

note as N10
  SetLayerPropsCommand: rename (Enter / focus loss), eye toggle (one click), opacity slider (on release). new() returns None when nothing differs.
    apply : frame.set_layer_props(layer_id, after)      revert: frame.set_layer_props(layer_id, before)
  ResizeCanvasCommand: created by the import flow when the user accepts "Resize project". Grow only (after.cols >= before.cols and after.rows >= before.rows).
    apply : project.resize_canvas(after)     revert: project.resize_canvas(before)
    The revert is lossless: History is strictly LIFO, so every command that could have written outside `before` has already been reverted.
  Import = CompositeCommand("Import file") [ ResizeCanvasCommand (only when the user accepted), AddLayerCommand::with_layer ] executed with
    execute_with_selection, so ONE Ctrl+Z removes the layer, shrinks the canvas back and restores the selection.
  Paste = AddLayerCommand::with_layer executed with execute_with_selection.
  Cut = CellPatchCommand "Cut" (the copy itself is not undoable and not dirty-making).
end note

